# Goal 11: Fix cpowf — precision loss inherited from sinf

## Function
- `cpowf` (complex float power)

## Source Files
- C: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/complexf/cpowf.c`
- Rust: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/complexf.rs` line ~345 (cpowf)

## Problem
MISMATCH: cpowf produces an incorrect imaginary part.

Failing test:
- cpowf((0,1),(2,0)): C returns (-1, -0x1.777a5cp-24), Rust returns (-1, -0x1.6bff7ap-16)

The imaginary part error (-0x1.6bff7ap-16 vs -0x1.777a5cp-24) is the exact same
discrepancy as the sinf bug (Goal 10). cpowf((0+i),(2+0i)) = i^2 = -1, and the
imaginary part involves sin(pi) which is the same failing input.

## What Needs to Change
This is almost certainly caused by the same sinf/trig precision bug as Goal 10.
Fix sinf first (Goal 10), then verify cpowf is also corrected.
If cpowf still fails after sinf is fixed, investigate cpowf independently.

## Success Criteria
- cpowf((0,1),(2,0)) = (-1, -0x1.777a5cp-24) — bitwise exact
